## Official logos from Wikimedia Commons (D399, 2026-10-16)

Fetched 2026-10-16 from Wikimedia Commons only (the Commons API's
`imageinfo`, then the original SVG from upload.wikimedia.org). Each SVG was
drawn in a headless Edge at 512 px with every shape filled in one ink, cropped
to the mark, scaled to fit 120 x 120 (Lanczos) and saved as lossless WebP. Nothing
else was changed: no redrawing, no shape edits.

**Licence and trademark.** Commons files each of these as **public domain**
(a logo of simple text and geometry, below the threshold of originality) and
marks every one **trademarked**. Public domain covers copyright only. The marks
stay the trademarks of their owners (Sony Interactive Entertainment, Nintendo),
and the app uses them only to name the console a config plays on (nominative
use). It never uses them as ZeroStick's own brand or to suggest endorsement.

| File(s) | Row | Commons file | Original | Author / owner | Licence on Commons |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| playstation-ink-dark.webp, playstation-ink-light.webp | PlayStation 5 (P5General dongle) | [File:PlayStation logo.svg](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlayStation_logo.svg) | https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/00/PlayStation_logo.svg | Sony Interactive Entertainment | Public domain; trademarked |
| ps3-ink-dark.webp, ps3-ink-light.webp | PS3 | [File:PlayStation 3 Logo.svg](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlayStation_3_Logo.svg) (the "PS3" wordmark) | https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d9/PlayStation_3_Logo.svg | Sony Computer Entertainment | Public domain; trademarked |
| switch-ink-dark.webp, switch-ink-light.webp | Nintendo Switch | [File:Nintendo Switch Logo (without text).svg](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nintendo_Switch_Logo_(without_text).svg) | https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/Nintendo_Switch_Logo_%28without_text%29.svg | Nintendo | Public domain; trademarked |
| switch2-ink-dark.webp, switch2-ink-light.webp | Nintendo Switch 2 | [File:Nintendo Switch 2 Logo (without text).svg](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nintendo_Switch_2_Logo_(without_text).svg) | https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f2/Nintendo_Switch_2_Logo_%28without_text%29.svg | Nintendo | Public domain; trademarked |

Why these files and not their neighbours on Commons. The PlayStation 3 row uses
the bare "PS3" wordmark, not the 2009 logo with "PlayStation 3" set under it
(that line would be unreadable at 26 px). The Switch rows use the "without text"
marks, not the red square with "NINTENDO SWITCH" written on it, so that they
read at row size and take the same two inks as the PlayStation marks.

Mirror has no logo and keeps the plug.
